            "description": "Watch Bolton Wanderers vs Stockport County highlights and goals from League One on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 24, 2026. Bolton Wanderers and Stockport County faced off in a high-stakes League One encounter on May 24, 2026 , delivering a match filled with tactical intensity. The game provided a rollercoaster of momentum shifts as both sides looked to establish dominance early on. Early Strikes and Tactical Battles The match ignited almost immediately when Bolton Wanderers took the lead in the 3rd minute. Ruben Rodrigues showed clinical composure to find the back of the net, giving the home fans an early reason to celebrate. However, Stockport County proved resilient and worked their way back into the contest. Their persistence paid off in the 29th minute as Odin Bailey turned provider for Adama Sidibeh , who struck a well-placed finish to level the score. The remainder of the first half was a balanced affair, with both teams searching for a breakthrough that remained elusive until the break. Momentum Shifts and Defensive Misfortune The second half saw the game turn on a series of critical moments. After Kyle Wootton received a yellow card in the 60th minute, disaster struck for the visitor just four minutes later when he inadvertently sent the ball into his own net. This own goal handed the lead back to Bolton and shifted the psychological advantage. Stockport attempted to reshape their side with multiple substitutions, but Bolton remained focused. In the 81st minute, Sam Dalby extended the lead after being set up by John McAtee , effectively putting the result beyond doubt as the match entered its closing stages. Late Red Card and Penalty Seal the Win Drama peaked in stoppage time as Stockport’s discipline evaporated. In the 90+2nd minute, Josh Dacres-Cogley was shown a straight red card , sparking heavy protests from his teammates. Exploiting the chaos, Bolton earned a penalty shortly after. Ruben Rodrigues stepped up in the 90+4th minute to convert from the spot, marking his second goal of the day and finalizing a 4-1 victory. The referee finally blew the whistle after eleven minutes of added time, concluding a professional and high-energy performance from the hosts."
